 36AR c  Compiled by J. Chen (NSCL, MSU): January 21, 2015                      
 36AR c  2015Su01: {+36,37}Ca beams were produced via the projectile            
 36AR2c  fragmentation reaction of {+9}Be({+40}Ca,X). E=69.42 MeV/nucleon       
 36AR3c  {+40}Ca primary beam with an intensity of 40 enA was produced from the 
 36AR4c  radioactive ion beam line at the Heavy Ion Research Facility in Lanzhou
 36AR5c  (HIRFL-RIBLL), impinging on a 990-|mm-thick {+9}Be target. Fragments   
 36AR6c  were identified by means of energy loss (|DE) and time of flight (tof) 
 36AR7c  with a 299-|mm-thick quadrant silicon detector and implanted into a    
 36AR8c  525-|mm-thick double-sided silicon strip detector as a |bp detector,   
 36AR9c  followed by three veto quadrant silicon detectors for the penetrating  
 36ARac  light particles. |g rays were detected by four segmented clover        
 36ARbc  detectors surrounding the DSSD. Measured Ep, Ip, |b-delayed p|g-coin,  
 36ARdc  decay-time spectra. Deduced T{-1/2}, |b-delayed proton decay energies  
 36ARec  and decay branching ratios.                                            
